+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "# Domains labeling\n",
+    "\n",
+    "When running `model.assign_domains`, the output domains are identified only by opaque IDs such as `D1003`, `L4`, and similar IDs. While sufficient for computation, these identifiers are difficult to interpret biologically.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "ℹ️ In practice, it is often preferable to replace them with biologically meaningful annotations such as 'Tertiary Lymphoid Structure' or 'Necrotic Tumor'.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This tutorial demonstrates a two-stage workflow for assigning interpretable domain names:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "1. 🔁 Automated pre-annotation using an LLM (guided by extracted marker signals per domain).\n",
+    "2. 🧑‍💻 Biology-guided manual review (optional but recommended) to validate and refine the proposed labels.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 1,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import novae"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Get the spatial domains\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Here, we assume you already ran `model.assign_domains`. If not, refer to the other tutorials, e.g. the [main usage tutorial](../main_usage) until you have your (unlabeled) spatial domains.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "> For the sake of the tutorial, we load a dataset that was pre-annotated, see below.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 2,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stderr",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "\u001b[36;20m[INFO] (novae.data._load._hf)\u001b[0m Found 1 h5ad file(s) matching the filters.\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "adata = novae.load_dataset(\"Xenium_V1_hPancreas_Cancer_Add_on_FFPE_outs\", annotations=True)[0]"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Note that this `AnnData` object already contains the following keys in `adata.obs`:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "- `cell_type` and `cell_type_level1`: a coarse and a detailed cell-type annotation (we used [scConcept](https://github.com/theislab/scConcept) and a [CELLxGENE](https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/) reference dataset).\n",
+    "- `novae_domains_res0.8` and `novae_domains_res1`: novae domains (unlabeled), obtained in zero-shot mode with a `resolution=0.8` and `resolution=1` respectively.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 3,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/plain": [
+       "['cell_type', 'cell_type_level1', 'novae_domains_res0.8', 'novae_domains_res1']"
+      ]
+     },
+     "execution_count": 3,
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "execute_result"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "adata.obs.columns[-4:].tolist()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "We see the domains are named `L0` to `L7`. We would like to provide meaningful labels instead!\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 4,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/plain": [
+       "novae_domains_res1\n",
+       "L0    45299\n",
+       "L5    26733\n",
+       "L3    25777\n",
+       "L4    24055\n",
+       "L2    23553\n",
+       "L6    22224\n",
+       "L1    13647\n",
+       "L7     9666\n",
+       "Name: count, dtype: int64"
+      ]
+     },
+     "execution_count": 4,
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "execute_result"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "adata.obs[\"novae_domains_res1\"].value_counts()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Automated labeling\n",
+    "\n",
+    "You can use [`novae.label_domains`](../../api/label/#novae.label_domains) to generate a DataFrame mapping each domain ID to a domain label.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "### API key setup\n",
+    "\n",
+    "An API key is required to use this function. You can either provide it directly as an `api_key` argument to [`novae.label_domains`](../../api/label/#novae.label_domains), or set it as an environment variable (`OPENAI_API_KEY` for OpenAI, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for Anthropic).\n",
+    "\n",
+    "> If you just want to generate the prompt without making an API call, set `return_prompt=True` and no API key will be required. You can then copy/paste the generated `messages` and `output_schema` into your preferred LLM playground.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For this example, we decided to load an `OPENAI_API_KEY` variable that we saved in a `.env` file:\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 2,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/plain": [
+       "True"
+      ]
+     },
+     "execution_count": 2,
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "execute_result"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "import dotenv\n",
+    "\n",
+    "dotenv.load_dotenv(\"./.env\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### LLM call\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Then, we can actually run the labeling. Internally, it uses an LLM that is prompted with descriptive information: DEGs per domain, domain sizes, and optionally pathway expressions or cell-type proportions.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "See more details in the [API](../../api/label/#novae.label_domains) on how to add pathway/cell-type information or LLM arguments.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 6,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "df_labels = novae.label_domains(\n",
+    "    adata,\n",
+    "    \"novae_domains_res1\",  # the column in adata.obs containing the domain IDs to label\n",
+    "    tissue=\"pancreas-cancer\",  # optional context (tissue or disease name)\n",
+    "    species=\"human\",  # optional context (species name)\n",
+    ")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "It creates a DataFrame with a label associated to each domain ID and a confidence score:\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 7,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/html": [
