+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Usage on multiple slides\n",
+    "\n",
+    "If you have multiple slides, you still need to run `novae.label_domains` **only once**, since Novae was designed to retreive the same domains across slides.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Simply choose to run `novae.label_domains` on a representative slide (i.e., containing all domains), and then apply the `.map` for each slide.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "adatas = ...  # multiple AnnData / slides\n",
+    "adata_representative = ...  # on slide among the list\n",
+    "\n",
+    "# run once (on the representative slide)\n",
+    "df_labels = novae.label_domains(adata_representative, \"novae_domains_res1\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "for adata in adatas:\n",
+    "    adata.obs[\"novae_domains_labeled\"] = adata.obs[\"novae_domains_res1\"].map(df_labels[\"label\"])"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Manual review\n",
+    "\n",
+    "We recommend to validate and refine the proposed labels. This requires biological knowledge, but allows a greater confidence in the resulting labels.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For the sake of the tutorial, we show it on another slide - as an extra example - but the steps apply to any slides / tissues.\n"
